course: dictionary
lesson: 7872
title: Rainy and the rainy season
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rainy is an adjective. It describes a noun and tells you there is a lot of rain: a rainy day, a rainy country. «A girl in Vancouver is bored on a rainy Saturday with no screens» tells you the day is wet, so she is stuck indoors.
explain: Look at the words around rainy to be sure of its meaning. A rainy season is the time of year when it rains most. «Every rainy season the Amazon rises by up to ten metres or more» tells you the river rises at the time of year when the rain falls most.
explain: Rainy is also part of phrases. «A rainy day» means a time of trouble, so to save for a rainy day means to put money aside for bad times. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it: save money for when you will need it.
fact: Rainy means with a lot of rain.
fact: A rainy season is the time of year when it rains most.
fact: Tropical places often have a rainy season and a dry season.
fact: «Lovely weather for ducks» is a cheerful joke about rain.
exercise: «A girl in Vancouver is bored on a rainy Saturday with no screens.» What does rainy mean here? | *Wet, with a lot of rain | Sunny and hot | Cold and snowy | Very loud
exercise: What is a rainy season? | A week with no school | *A time of year when it rains most | A time of year when the sun shines most | A day with lots of wind
exercise: «Save for a rainy day» means | Spend all your money today | *Save money for bad times that may come | Buy a new umbrella | Go for a walk whenever it rains
test: Which is the comparative form of rainy? | *rainier | rainyer | more rainy | rainyest
test: Pat says «Lovely weather for ducks, chuck!» on rainy days. What is she doing? | *Making a cheerful joke about the rain | The ducks are lost | Warning them about the wind | Telling the children to go to the lake
exam: Which phrase means a time of trouble, as in «a rainy day fund»? | Rainy season | *A rainy day | Sunny afternoon | Wet socks
